---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { siteFromHost } from '../../content';
const site = siteFromHost();
const path = '/compare/postscript-vs-attentive';
const title = "Postscript vs Attentive for Shopify: 2026 Comparison";
const desc = "Compare channel consolidation and operating control A Shopify workflow and migration comparison, with current supplier sources.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Is Attentive only for enterprise retailers?",
    "answer": "Use demonstrated account controls and contract terms to assess fit. Revenue bands and team size alone cannot establish which platform meets your requirements."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does either product replace email?",
    "answer": "Attentive offers Email. Postscript has announced Email with a waitlist. Confirm access and required workflows rather than assuming either is SMS-only or automatically a complete replacement."
  },
  {
    "question": "Which is safer for compliance?",
    "answer": "This comparison establishes no legal or compliance ranking. Review your capture language, subscription records, opt-out handling and operator controls for each intended market with appropriate counsel."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-14 md:py-20">
    <div class="container">
      <nav class="mb-8 text-sm"><a class="link" href="/compare">Comparisons</a></nav>
      <header class="max-w-4xl"><p class="editorial-kicker">Head-to-head</p><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Postscript vs Attentive for Shopify</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">Compare channel consolidation and operating control</p></header>
      <article class="prose-shopify mt-14 max-w-4xl">
        <h2>Both shortlists now need an email question</h2>
        <p>Attentive markets an <a href="https://www.attentive.com/email-marketing">email platform</a> as well as SMS. The old description of two SMS-only products is incomplete. Decide whether you are selecting a text sender or replacing email and text together; the latter also requires template, sender-domain and historical-data migration.</p>
        <h2>Evaluate governance as a requirement, not a revenue band</h2>
        <p>A single Shopify brand can need strict approval controls; a large retailer can run a narrow text program. List the people who can edit audiences, approve offers, export records and pause sends. Ask both suppliers to demonstrate those exact permissions in the proposed account. Do not infer a compliance winner from an enterprise label or a store’s annual revenue.</p>
        <h2>Use an online and store-capture exercise</h2>
        <p>Proposed exercise, not a reported test: submit the same customer through a Shopify form and a retail QR campaign, then inspect identity matching, source labels and subscription history. Repeat with different email addresses sharing a phone number. Confirm that an unsubscribe remains effective after another import and that staff can explain which record controls eligibility.</p>
        <h2>Make launch coordination observable</h2>
        <p>For a product drop, document eligible recipients, inventory exclusions, scheduled messages and who may stop the launch. Ask the operator to change an offer and exclude recent buyers in a draft. Review whether approvals and pending journeys update as intended. Do not use an arbitrary time-to-edit target as a product ranking; set the required deadline from your real campaign process.</p>
        <h2>Inspect reply ownership and escalation</h2>
        <p>For text conversations, request a demonstration of the receiving inbox, assignment and handoff to support. Try an order-status question, an opt-out and a product question requiring specialist advice. Specify coverage outside staffed hours and the response a shopper sees. Conversational selling is useful only if the team can support the promises made in the message; this page reports no comparative reply-speed test.</p>
        <h2>Price the contract and the migration separately</h2>
        <p>Give both suppliers the same expected channel volumes, destination countries and peak calendar. Request included usage, overages, carrier-related charges, onboarding scope, support terms, renewal dates and cancellation obligations. Include the labor of preserving email templates and rebuilding retail capture. There is no evidenced universal send-volume point where one supplier becomes cheaper.</p>
        <h2>Choose the scope your team can operate</h2>
        <p>If the existing email platform meets requirements, compare text-only proposals before expanding the project. If unifying email and SMS is the objective, require evidence that the combined journeys and permissions work for your brands and locations. Keep procurement controls, reply staffing and financial terms as separate decision criteria; a strength in one does not establish superiority in the others.</p>
        <h2>Postscript scope and evidence limits</h2>
        <p>Postscript describes <a href="https://postscript.io/features">Shopify SMS workflows</a> and has announced <a href="https://postscript.io/email">Postscript Email with a waitlist</a>. Confirm account access before retiring an email sender. Supplier descriptions checked November 25, 2026; no live account tests, performance results or compliance ranking are claimed here.</p>
      </article>
      <div class="mt-10 max-w-4xl text-sm">
        <p class="font-black text-[#24170f]">Related comparisons</p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          <a class="link" href="/compare/klaviyo-vs-postscript">Klaviyo vs Postscript</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/omnisend-vs-attentive">Omnisend vs Attentive</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/compare/postscript-vs-smsbump">Postscript vs SMSBump</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/for/beauty">Email apps for beauty stores</a> ·
          <a class="link" href="/use-cases/abandoned-cart">Abandoned cart playbook</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} title="Postscript vs Attentive FAQ" />
</BaseLayout>
